      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: Ummmm, did the yt-dlp update actually go through yet? The video provided in the canny still isn't loading in VRChat. Both USharp Video and ProTV just say \"invalid url\". \n\nI tried manually deleting the yt-dlp.exe to let it re-download and reinstalled VRC. And it still won't play. Other videos are also still having issues.\n\nHere's the also the logs from when I try to play the video. Don't know if it's useful or not, but I might as well:\n\n \n\n2022.12.12 19:45:15 Log        -  [USharpVideo] Started video load for URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XTPTmKIocSM, requested by Fizzytaco\n\n2022.12.12 19:45:15 Log        -  [Video Playback] Attempting to resolve URL 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XTPTmKIocSM'\n\n2022.12.12 19:45:15 Log        -  NativeProcess.Start: started process id [9948]: C:/Users/aaaaaa/AppData/LocalLow/VRChat/VRChat\\Tools/yt-dlp.exe (...)\n\n2022.12.12 19:45:18 Log        -  NativeProcess.HasExited: process exited with code 0, took 2497 ms. Command line: C:/Users/aaaaaa/AppData/LocalLow/VRChat/VRChat\\Tools/yt-dlp.exe (...)\n\n2022.12.12 19:45:18 Error      -  [Video Playback] yt_dlp\\jsinterp.pyc:346: FutureWarning: Possible nested set at position 3\n\n2022.12.12 19:45:18 Log        -  [Video Playback] URL 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XTPTmKIocSM' resolved to 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XTPTmKIocSM'\n\n2022.12.12 19:45:18 Error      -  [USharpVideo] Video 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XTPTmKIocSM' failed to play with error InvalidURL",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
